Use case: identity-preserve. Production pixel-art animation asset for a 2D fighting game.
Use the approved Shiori seed character in the two references. Keep her peach-blonde braids, face, turquoise palette, same sports costume and pale athletic boots. Adult professional martial-arts competitor, neutral nonsexual action presentation, full body visible.
Replace the empty transparent edit canvas with ONE spritesheet of exactly 4 columns and 4 rows, 16 independent full-body figures facing RIGHT. Each row is one airborne attack, each column startup, active extension, recoil, recovery:
row 1 airborne palm strike;
row 2 horizontal airborne boot kick with the other knee tucked;
row 3 downward angled airborne boot kick;
row 4 diagonal diving kick with upper body balancing backwards.
The first pose has a long rear leg pointing down so body scale can be calibrated. Other poses have naturally bent airborne knees. Keep identical head-to-hip length, torso size, outfit details and pixel clusters across all frames. Pelvis stays at a consistent slot position. Leave clear transparent gutters between whole figures, never crop hands/feet/hair. Crisp native pixel art matching the seed, detailed yet readable face, strong attack silhouettes.
Transparent RGBA background, no floor, no shadows, no scenery, no effects, no labels, no text, no watermark. No close-ups or exaggerated anatomy. Preferred canvas1792x1792.
